# ---- Private source material. Never publish. -------------------------------
# The original art dump. Contains a saved ChatGPT conversation export
# (n:i-us & vc walk cycles.html + its _files bundle) and a desktop screenshot,
# i.e. personal data that has no business in a public repo. It is also 209 MB
# and nothing at runtime reads it.
assets/assets:vietnam/

# Dead pipeline. The V3 cut-out approach is retired (see SPRITE_PIPELINE.md §1);
# 70 MB of source figures kept only for archaeology.
assets/v3_sources/

# ---- Build artifacts. Regenerated by tools/, not sources. -------------------
# Individual rendered frames. The game loads atlas.png/atlas.json only; these are
# ~40 MB of intermediate output from tools/render_model_sprites.py.
assets/sprites3d/*/*_[0-9][0-9].png
assets/sprites3d/*/index.json
assets/sprites3d/*/.outlined.json

# NOT assets/props/.toned.json — it used to be ignored here as a build artifact,
# which it is not. The prop PNGs ARE committed and they are committed ALREADY
# GRADED, so the ledger is the only thing standing between a fresh clone and
# tools/tone_props.py grading them a second time: 0.80 twice is 0.64, and a
# second 4px rim on top of the first is an 8px black border. The sprite ledgers
# above are genuinely disposable because the frames they guard are not committed.

# Debug captures and contact sheets written during development.
assets/debug/

# ---- Local noise -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.vercel
node_modules/

# Seeded design-canvas output. 2.2 MB of editor payload, regenerated from the
# .dc.html sources beside it; the canvas itself lives as a published Artifact.
# The sources ARE tracked — they are the design; this file is a build product,
# and it would otherwise be served from the live site for no reason.
design/hud/*.html
!design/hud/*.dc.html

# ---- Credentials. Never commit. --------------------------------------------
# .env.local was TRACKED and reached the public repo in the very first commit,
# carrying a Vercel OIDC token. That token had already expired (2026-07-07) by
# the time it was found, so there was no live exposure — but it was published,
# and the only reason it did no harm is that it aged out. Anything matching
# these patterns stays out of git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
